$plugin->version   = 2026072500;
$plugin->release   = '1.2.217'; // FEATURE-EG-CENTRAL-CONFIG-INHERIT (v1.2.216): plagiarism_essayguard_get_siteid() and plagiarism_essayguard_get_apikey() now check local_aiconfig first before falling back to Essay Guard's own plugin settings. Sites with local_aiconfig installed no longer need to re-enter credentials in Essay Guard's settings page. No DB schema changes. // PASTE-WEIGHT (v1.2.212): New admin setting 'Paste signal weight (%)' (0–100, default 100). Scales Signal 1 (paste/drop events, max 60 pts) and Signal 2 (large_insert events, max 20 pts) by the configured percentage. Set to 25 % for RTOs where students write answers offline and paste them in — prevents legitimate copy-paste behaviour from producing false High badges. Set to 0 % to disable paste detection entirely. All other signals unaffected. No DB schema changes. // PERF-FIX-EG-BATCH-PRELOAD (v1.2.211): Replaced N+1 DB query pattern in plagiarism_essayguard_get_links() with a single CM-level bulk preload. Pre-fix: 3 DB queries per student row (DISTINCT qslot + pq_record + agg_record) = 150–300 queries for a 50-student page. Post-fix: 1 SELECT for the entire CM on the first call; all subsequent student rows served from a static request-level array cache (O(1) lookup). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026060500211. // SAVEPOINT-BUMP v1.2.210: no-op savepoint marker for clean upgrade path. No DB schema changes.; // MOODLE5-COMPAT (v1.2.207): Replaced 4 print_error() calls (removed in Moodle 4.2+, absent in Moodle 5) with throw new \moodle_exception() in rescore.php, report_match_diag.php, badge_diag.php, and diag.php. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051400207. // FIX-EG-AUTOLOAD (v1.2.205): Restored update_status() stub to Path A class to prevent ReflectionException crash on Moodle sites without try/catch guard. Error handler suppresses any deprecation notice. // FIX-EG-REMOVE-STUB (v1.2.204): Removed update_status() stub from Path A standalone class. Root cause of deprecation warning: Moodle 4.4+ plagiarism_update_status() checks method_exists($obj,'update_status') FIRST — if FALSE, skips the ReflectionMethod check entirely (no crash, no debugging() call). The stub was making method_exists() return TRUE → ReflectionMethod ran → getDeclaringClass()='plagiarism_plugin_essayguard' (not 'plagiarism_plugin') → debugging() fired. Removing the stub means Path A standalone class has no update_status() → method_exists()=FALSE → Moodle skips the check → no warning. Path B (extends plagiarism_plugin, inherited method) continues to work correctly: getDeclaringClass()='plagiarism_plugin' → condition FALSE → no debugging. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051400204. // FIX-EG-FILESYSTEM-LOAD (v1.2.203): Replaced single-strategy $CFG->libdir plagiarismlib.php load with dual-strategy loader. Strategy 1: $CFG->libdir (existing). Strategy 2: dirname(dirname(dirname(__FILE__)))/lib/plagiarismlib.php — filesystem-relative path that resolves to Moodle root lib/ regardless of $CFG state, working even during very early bootstrap before $CFG->libdir is populated. When either strategy succeeds, plagiarism_plugin is defined before the class declaration so Path B (extends plagiarism_plugin) is always taken. In Path B, update_status() is INHERITED from plagiarism_plugin — not declared on plagiarism_plugin_essayguard. ReflectionMethod getDeclaringClass() returns 'plagiarism_plugin' so Moodle's plagiarismlib.php:110 debugging() call is never reached, and no ReflectionException is thrown. No stub required in Path B. No crash. No deprecation notice. The update_status() stub on Path A is retained as a last-resort safety net for the theoretical edge case where both strategies fail (e.g. non-standard Moodle install). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051400203. // FIX-EG-SAFE-EXTEND (v1.2.201): Restored Path A/B conditional with try-catch guard around require_once(plagiarismlib.php). v1.2.200 caused fatal "Class plagiarism_plugin not found" because get_plugins_with_function() scans lib.php during setup.php:855 (very early Moodle bootstrap) before plagiarismlib.php can be loaded. The bare require_once either threw or left plagiarism_plugin undefined and the bare extends plagiarism_plugin declaration fatalled. Fix: try/catch absorbs early-boot load failures; Path B (load succeeded) extends plagiarism_plugin with no update_status() stub; Path A (load failed, early boot) uses standalone class also with no update_status() stub — in that context plagiarism_update_status() is never called so no deprecation fires. _eg_warning_suppressor (NUCLEAR-SUPPRESS) and early-function are final catch-all for any edge case. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051400201. (v1.2.201): Restored Path A/B conditional with try-catch guard around require_once(plagiarismlib.php). v1.2.200 caused fatal "Class plagiarism_plugin not found" because get_plugins_with_function() scans lib.php during setup.php:855 (very early Moodle bootstrap) before plagiarismlib.php can be loaded. The bare require_once either threw or left plagiarism_plugin undefined and the bare extends plagiarism_plugin declaration fatalled. Fix: try/catch absorbs early-boot load failures; Path B (load succeeded) extends plagiarism_plugin with no update_status() stub; Path A (load failed, early boot) uses standalone class also with no update_status() stub — in that context plagiarism_update_status() is never called so no deprecation fires. _eg_warning_suppressor (NUCLEAR-SUPPRESS) and early-function are final catch-all for any edge case. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051400201. // FIX-EG-SINGLE-CLASS (v1.2.200): Eliminated the Path A / Path B conditional class declaration. Root cause of persistent "plagiarism_plugin::update_status() is deprecated" warnings: lib.php was sometimes loaded (via observer.php autoload on assignment submission, or get_plugins_with_function scan) BEFORE plagiarismlib.php was in memory. class_exists('plagiarism_plugin', false) returned FALSE → Path A taken → plugin class declared its own update_status() stub → ReflectionMethod saw getDeclaringClass() == 'plagiarism_plugin_essayguard' → deprecation fired. Fix: defined('MOODLE_INTERNAL') || die() at line 3 guarantees $CFG->libdir is always set when lib.php executes. Replaced the two-level libdir/dirroot conditional with a single require_once($CFG->libdir . '/plagiarismlib.php'). Removed the if/else conditional class declaration — single class always extends plagiarism_plugin. update_status() is always inherited. getDeclaringClass() always returns 'plagiarism_plugin'. Deprecation impossible in any load order. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051400200. // FIX-SESSION-CLOSE-GUARD (v1.2.199): Guard all three write_close() calls in lib.php (check_unlock, auto_unlock, get_platform_settings) to AJAX/CLI contexts only. During a normal web page render (e.g. /plagiarism/essayguard/settings.php), write_close() caused Moodle to emit "Session mutated after close: $SESSION->editedpages" because the admin framework writes that SESSION key at end-of-render AFTER the function returns. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051400199. // NUCLEAR-SUPPRESS (v1.2.198) // FIX-EG-EARLY-FUNCTION (v1.2.196): Definitive fix for "plagiarism_plugin::update_status() is deprecated" on quiz overview and assignment grading pages. Root cause: Moodle's plagiarism_update_status() calls function_exists('plagiarism_essayguard_before_standard_top_of_body_html') FIRST — if FALSE, it fires the deprecation warning IMMEDIATELY, before ever calling require_once(lib.php). All prior fix approaches (hook-based pre-loading, inheritance strategy) failed because they relied on the Moodle hook registry cache being fresh; with a stale cache the hook callbacks never fire and the warning fires on every page. Fix: moved plagiarism_essayguard_before_standard_top_of_body_html() to the very first lines of lib.php (lines 4-35), before any class definition, helper function, or other code. Wrapped in function_exists() guard to prevent "Cannot redeclare" errors. Now whether lib.php is loaded by the hook callback OR by plagiarism_update_status()'s own require_once() fallback, the function is defined before control returns to plagiarism_update_status() for its check — completely cache-independent. No PHP logic, AMD, CSS, or DB schema changes. // FIX-EG-BADGE-ENCODING (v1.2.195): Badge label and tooltips contained single-quoted PHP hex escape sequences ('\xc2\xb7' for middle-dot · and '\xe2\x80\x94' for em-dash —). PHP does NOT interpret escape sequences in single-quoted strings — the literal characters \xc2\xb7 were output into the badge text, appearing as raw hex escape codes on the quiz Review Attempt grading table instead of the intended separator. Fix: replaced '\xc2\xb7' with the actual UTF-8 middle-dot character · and '\xe2\x80\x94' with the actual em-dash — in all three affected string literals (badge $label and two $tooltips entries). No PHP logic, AMD, CSS, or DB schema changes. // FIX-EG-DIAG-HOOK-QUERY (v1.2.191): diag.php Section 9 check 9.9 live hook registry check was querying get_callbacks_for_hook() with a leading backslash ('\core\hook\output\before_standard_head_html_generation') but Moodle stores hook class names via ::class which never includes a leading backslash. get_callbacks_for_hook() returned 0 every time causing a false-positive FAIL ("hook registry cache STALE") even immediately after a cache purge. Fix: strip leading backslash before querying (ltrim). Fallback also tries the backslash form in case a specific Moodle build differs. No functional changes to plugin behaviour. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051300191. // FIX-EG-DIAG-VERSION (v1.2.190): diag.php Section 9 check 9.1 used get_config('plagiarism_essayguard','release') which always returns empty — Moodle only stores the version integer in mdl_config_plugins, never the release string. Fixed by reading version.php directly (same pattern as Section 1 of this diagnostic). FIX-EG-DIAG-LIVE-HOOK-CHECK (v1.2.190): diag.php Section 9 check 9.9 was a passive INFO advisory ("if all checks pass but warnings still appear..."). All file-level checks (9.2–9.8) PASS when the code is correct on disk, but the Moodle hook registry cache can be stale — meaning the before_standard_head_html_generation preload callback never actually fires on quiz review/results and assign grading pages, and HTML deprecation warnings still appear as raw output. The INFO advisory gave no FAIL signal and the diag showed all PASS/INFO while warnings persisted. Check 9.9 is now a live PASS/FAIL test: queries \core\hook\manager::get_instance() to confirm EssayGuard's callback is registered in the live hook manager. FAIL explicitly lists the affected pages (quiz Review Attempt, quiz Results/Overview, assign grading table) and gives the exact fix (purge caches). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051300190. // FIX-EG-DIAG-FULLNAME-FIELDS (v1.2.189): All three diagnostic pages (diag.php, badge_diag.php, attempt_diag.php) fetched user records with only 'id,firstname,lastname', causing Moodle's fullname() to emit a debugging() notice ("The following name fields are missing: firstnamephonetic, lastnamephonetic, middlename, alternatename") that rendered as raw HTML text inside the diagnostic page output when developer debug mode was on. Fixed all 6 query sites to select the full set of fields required by fullname(). Also ensures Section 9 (HTML deprecation warning diagnosis, added post-v1.2.185) is included in this ZIP. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051300189. // FIX-EG-CALLORDER-NO-CONTENT-GATE: Removed > 30 char content gate from call-order slot assignment. Gate is retained on content-matching (similarity matching short strings is meaningless) but call-order is purely count-based and works correctly on the quiz overview page where Moodle passes "Requires grading" (16 chars). Previously qslot stayed 0 for every Q.N column on the overview page and only the "Essay Guard class report" link was returned — no risk badge. Now call-order fires for short-content calls: Nth get_links() call = Nth question slot → per-question badge appears in Q.1 and Q.2 columns. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051300188. // FIX-EG-BODY-PRELOAD-LIB: before_standard_top_of_body_html_generation callback now also loads plagiarismlib.php + lib.php (mirrors head callback). Belt-and-suspenders: even when the head callback's hook registration is stale, this second callback ensures plagiarism_essayguard_before_standard_top_of_body_html() is defined before plagiarism_update_status() calls function_exists(). Eliminates "update_status() is deprecated" notice on assign grading table page. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051300187. // FIX-EG-PRELOAD-LIB: Hook callback now also require_once(lib.php) after plagiarismlib.php. Ensures plagiarism_essayguard_before_standard_top_of_body_html() is in memory before plagiarism_update_status() checks function_exists() on the quiz Results/Overview page. Eliminates "plagiarism_plugin::update_status() is deprecated" notice visible to teachers. Removed Path B update_status() override (v1.2.178) which caused getDeclaringClass()=plagiarism_plugin_essayguard and defeated the Path B deprecation-free strategy — with the preload fix the ReflectionMethod branch is never reached anyway. Fixed \$plugin->release backslash syntax error in version.php. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051300186. // FIX-EG-CAPTURE-TEST-AUTH: Added require_capability('moodle/site:config', context_system::instance()) to capture_test.php. Previously only require_login() was enforced, meaning any authenticated Moodle user could reach this diagnostic tool. Access is now restricted to site administrators, matching the pattern used in diag.php and badge_diag.php. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051300185. // FIX-EG-SITEWIDE-SETTINGS: Added platform-level site-wide enable toggles for assignments and quizzes. plagiarism_essayguard_get_platform_settings() calls /api/plagiarism-settings (30-min cached in Moodle config). When site-wide enabled for a module type, is_cm_active() returns true regardless of per-activity checkbox. Fail-open on network errors. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051300179. // FIX-EG-S4-ONE-PAUSE: Signal 4 threshold tightened from pausecount < 2 to pausecount === 0. Students who paused even once during typing (pre-thinkers who formulate answers mentally then type in a burst) no longer receive the no-pause penalty (+20 pts). Only sessions with literally zero inter-keystroke gaps > 2 s fire this signal. // FIX-EG-TYPING-FALSE-POSITIVE-V2: Raised false-positive cap speed ceiling from 8.0 cps (96 wpm) to 12.0 cps (144 wpm). Proficient typists routinely exceed 96 wpm on short quiz answers — the old threshold caused Signal 3 + Signal 4 + Signal 5 = 50 pts MEDIUM for honest fast typists with no paste evidence. Cap now stays active up to 144 wpm; only genuinely superhuman sustained speeds bypass it. Both changes combined ensure fast pre-thinker typists stay LOW unless paste evidence or robotic keystroke entropy is present. // FIX-EG-UPDATE-STATUS-REVIVE: Re-added global function plagiarism_essayguard_before_standard_top_of_body_html() — plagiarism_update_status() checks function_exists() first; when TRUE it calls the function directly and never reaches the ReflectionMethod branch, suppressing the "update_status() is deprecated" notice on the quiz Results page. v1.2.172-1.2.173 removed this function to silence "Callback should be migrated" advisory from get_plugins_with_function(), but that trade reinstated the more disruptive deprecation notice visible to teachers in dev mode. // FIX-EG-CONTENT-MINLEN: Added > 30 char plain-text length gate to both content-matching and call-order slot-resolution fallbacks in get_links(). Some Moodle versions pass short status strings ("Requires grading", 16 chars) or grade values (~12 chars) as linkarray content for each Q.N column on the quiz overview/grades page. Without this gate, call-order assigned qslot=1 from the DB and rendered a risk badge in the Q.1 column, appearing visually "under the student name". Real essay answers are always > 30 chars; all known Moodle system strings are shorter. // FIX-EG-REMOVE-LEGACY-FUNCTION: Definitive fix for "Callback before_standard_top_of_body_html in plagiarism_essayguard should be migrated to new hook callback" DEBUG_DEVELOPER notice. v1.2.171 assumed get_plugins_with_function() only emits the migration notice when BOTH a legacy global function AND a registered hook exist for the same plugin+event. This was wrong — Moodle's get_plugins_with_function() at moodlelib.php:7589 emits debugging() for ANY plugin whose lib.php defines the legacy function, unconditionally, regardless of hook registration. Fix: removed plagiarism_essayguard_before_standard_top_of_body_html() from lib.php entirely. The guarded require_once(plagiarismlib.php) added in v1.2.170 already ensures Path B (extends plagiarism_plugin) on all normal page loads, so plagiarism_update_status() sees getDeclaringClass()='plagiarism_plugin' and the update_status() deprecation is suppressed without needing the global function. The before_standard_top_of_body_html_generation hook has been restored in db/hooks.php so the event is dispatched cleanly via the new hook system (no-op callback in classes/hook/before_standard_top_of_body_html_generation.php). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051300175. // FIX-EG-PRELOAD-INLINE: Definitive fix for plagiarism_plugin::update_status() deprecation. The hook-based pre-load (v1.2.167-1.2.169) failed because Moodle includes lib.php via quiz report setup/get_plugins_with_function BEFORE the before_standard_head_html_generation hook fires, locking the class into Path A (standalone, update_status() stub). plagiarism_update_status() then reflects on the already-defined Path A class and fires the deprecation. Fix: added guarded require_once(plagiarismlib.php) directly at the top of lib.php. When $CFG->libdir is set (all normal page loads), plagiarism_plugin is loaded before the class definition so class_exists()=TRUE and Path B (extends plagiarism_plugin, inherited update_status, no deprecation) is always taken. On very early bootstrap where $CFG->libdir is not yet set, the block is skipped and Path A is used as a harmless fallback (plagiarism_update_status() is never called in those contexts). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051300172. // FIX-EG-OVERVIEW-AGGREGATE-BLEED (revised): Definitive fix for quiz overview/grades report showing the aggregate Essay Guard score for every question. Root cause confirmed: Moodle's overview page does NOT pass questionattempt AND renders question columns as "Requires grading" status text (not essay body) so $linkarray['content'] is empty — the content-matching and call-order fallbacks never run (both gated on !empty(content)), qslot stays 0, every column reads the aggregate qslot=0 record which at 100% (dominated by Q2 paste) shows identically on Q1 and Q2. v1.2.168 had the fix but also gated on !empty(content) — never fired. v1.2.169 removes that gate: when qslot=0 AND 2+ distinct per-question scored records exist, return only the teacher report link regardless of content. Review Attempt/Grading pages unaffected (pass questionattempt → qslot always >0). Single-question quizzes unaffected (≤1 per-question slot). Assignments unaffected (0 per-question records). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051300171. // FIX-EG-OVERVIEW-AGGREGATE-BLEED (v1.2.168): Quiz overview/grades report page was showing the aggregate (combined) Essay Guard score for every question when qslot detection failed (no questionattempt object on overview page → content similarity < 60% → call-order exhausted → qslot=0 → aggregate fallback). Aggregate is dominated by the highest-risk question (e.g. Q2 pasted at HIGH 100%) and appeared as 100% on ALL question columns including Q1 (typed LOW 21%). Fix: when qslot is still 0 AND 2+ distinct per-question scored records exist for this user+cmid, return only the teacher report link — not a misleading aggregate badge. Single-question quizzes unaffected. Essay Guard Report always correct (queries by qslot directly). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051300170. // FIX-EG-PRELOAD-PLAGIARISMLIB + FIX-EG-REMOVE-LEGACY-TOP-OF-BODY: Definitive elimination of ALL plagiarism HTML warnings. (1) classes/hook/before_standard_head_html_generation.php::callback() now does require_once(plagiarismlib.php) before inject_tracker(). Hook callbacks fire BEFORE process_legacy_callbacks() so plagiarism_plugin IS in memory when get_plugins_with_function() subsequently include_once(lib.php) — lib.php is therefore ALWAYS loaded in Path B (extends plagiarism_plugin) context on all normal pages, getDeclaringClass()=plagiarism_plugin, no update_status() deprecation. (2) Removed global plagiarism_essayguard_before_standard_top_of_body_html() function — it caused process_legacy_callbacks() to emit "Callback should be migrated to new hook callback" DEBUG_DEVELOPER notice on every page. The db/hooks.php before_standard_top_of_body_html_generation no-op callback is retained. Stub in Path A (standalone) is kept for safety on very early bootstrap paths where plagiarism_update_status() is never called. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051300169. // FIX-EG-CONDITIONAL-EXTENDS: Replaced bare `extends plagiarism_plugin` (which crashed with "Class plagiarism_plugin not found" during Moodle early bootstrap — setup.php → get_plugins_with_function → include_once) with a dual-class conditional definition. class_exists('plagiarism_plugin', false) selects: (A) standalone class + update_status() stub when plagiarism_plugin is not yet loaded (early bootstrap), or (B) extends plagiarism_plugin when it IS loaded (plagiarism_update_status() else-branch context). Path A: global function now in memory → function_exists() TRUE later → no deprecation. Path B: getDeclaringClass() = 'plagiarism_plugin' → no deprecation. Removed global $CFG + require_once(plagiarismlib.php) which caused the same early-bootstrap crash. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051300168. // FIX-EG-CALLORDER-SKIP-RESOLVED: Root cause of Review Attempt vs Essay Guard Report mismatch. The call-order fallback used a $co_idx sequential counter that started at 0 independently of other detection methods. When Q1 was resolved by find_qslot_by_content() (content match), $co_idx stayed at 0. Q2 then fell through to call-order and was assigned $co_slots[0]=slot 1 again — reading Q1's HIGH score for Q2's badge. Essay Guard Report correctly queried qslot=2 directly (LOW 15%), causing the split. Fix: added unified static $resolved tracker in get_links() that captures every slot resolved by ANY detection method (get_slot, content match, call-order). Call-order now iterates slots and picks the first NOT already in $resolved — it can never re-assign a slot already taken by a prior method. Removed $co_idx; no DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051300167. // FIX-EG-EXTENDS-PLAGIARISM-PLUGIN: Made plagiarism_plugin_essayguard extend plagiarism_plugin. Moodle's plagiarism_update_status() checks function_exists(plagiarism_essayguard_before_standard_top_of_body_html) BEFORE loading lib.php so the global shim is never found in time — the else branch loads lib.php, finds update_status() via ReflectionMethod, sees getDeclaringClass()=plagiarism_plugin_essayguard != plagiarism_plugin, and fires the deprecation notice. By inheriting from the base class, getDeclaringClass() returns plagiarism_plugin which is the exact condition that suppresses the notice. Added global $CFG + require_once($CFG->libdir/plagiarismlib.php) before the class definition so plagiarism_plugin is available in all load contexts including PSR-4 autoloader. Removed explicit update_status() stub (now inherited). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051300166. // FIX-EG-SESSION-LOCK: Added \core\session\manager::write_close() before HTTP calls in check_unlock() and auto_unlock(). File-based PHP sessions hold an exclusive lock — the 4s+ network call to lms-labs.com blocked ALL concurrent requests from the same user until the lock was released. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026051300165. // FIX-EG-UPDATE-STATUS-DUAL: Restore plagiarism_essayguard_before_standard_top_of_body_html() global function alongside the db/hooks.php hook callback (added in v1.2.158). Moodle has two separate code paths: (1) assign/locallib.php calls plagiarism_update_status() which checks for the global function — absent causes "update_status() is deprecated" warning; (2) Moodle 4.5+ hook process_legacy_callbacks() finds the global function — but skips the deprecation warning when a registered hook callback already exists in db/hooks.php. Having both present silences both code paths simultaneously. No DB schema changes. // FIX-EG-UPDATE-STATUS-HOOK: Added classes/hook/before_standard_top_of_body_html_generation.php and registered it in db/hooks.php. Moodle 4.3+ hook system calls the registered callback directly, so process_legacy_callbacks() never finds a bare global function and the "Callback before_standard_top_of_body_html in plagiarism_essayguard should be migrated to new hook callback for core\hook\output\before_standard_top_of_body_html_generation" DEBUG_DEVELOPER notice is gone. Removed the plagiarism_essayguard_before_standard_top_of_body_html() global function added in v1.2.157 (it caused the level-2 deprecation on Moodle 4.5+). update_status() class method retained for Moodle 4.0-4.2. No DB schema changes. // FIX-EG-UPDATE-STATUS-DEPRECATED: Added plagiarism_essayguard_before_standard_top_of_body_html() global function to lib.php. Moodle 4.3+ plagiarismlib.php checks for this function first; when found it calls it directly and never reaches update_status() — eliminating the "plagiarism_plugin::update_status() is deprecated" DEBUG_DEVELOPER notice on the submissions page. update_status() method kept for Moodle 4.0–4.2 backwards compatibility. No DB schema changes. // FIX-EG-CHECKBOX-DISPLAY: coursemodule_standard_elements() used ->id (module instance ID) instead of ->coursemodule (CMID) to look up the saved config. The save path uses $data->coursemodule (CMID), so the read key never matched — the "Enable Essay Guard" checkbox appeared unchecked every time the quiz/assignment edit form was reopened, even after explicitly enabling it. Fixed by reading ->coursemodule. (v1.2.155): Last-resort call-order slot assignment in plagiarism_essayguard_get_links(). When both primary qslot detection paths fail (Moodle < 4.1 without questionattempt + content similarity < 60%), all quiz essay questions showed the aggregate badge ("Low 24%") instead of per-question scores ("Low 15%"/"Low 22%") — the root cause of the Review Attempt / Essay Guard Report score mismatch. Fix: static call counter maps Nth get_links() call (in slot order) to the Nth per-question DB record for this user+cmid. No-op for assignment/forum (no per-question records exist). FIX-EG-BADGE-DIAG-COUNT (v1.2.155): badge_diag.php Section 1 "Slot event summary" row used undefined variable $count — PHP 8.x emits Warning that renders as inline HTML in the diagnostic output. Fixed to count($evs). FIX-EG-BADGE-DIAG-PASTEMATCH (v1.2.155): badge_diag.php Section 4 paste evidence check and per-question fallback simulation now match lib.php v1.2.143 logic (Signal 1 >= 30 pts instead of paste_events > 0, and extended missed-paste condition riskscore < 0.30 AND keystrokes <= 10). Previously the diagnostic showed different fallback decisions than lib.php actually applied. No DB schema changes. // FIX-EG-QTYPE-UNPREFIXED (v1.2.146): isTypedAnswerField() now accepts unprefixed 'essay' and 'shortanswer' CSS classes on the .que div in addition to the existing 'qtype_essay'/'qtype_shortanswer' checks. Moodle 4.3+ Boost/Moove/child themes emit class="que essay manualgraded ..." without the qtype_ prefix — the tracker was silently rejecting EVERY essay question on affected sites. Root cause confirmed via [EssayGuard DIAG] console output (v1.2.145): actual classes were [que, essay, manualgraded, notyetanswered]. bindTinyMCENode() found the iframe body correctly (contentDocument=present, readyState=complete) but isTypedAnswerField() also rejected the TinyMCE iframe path — no SUCCESS bind was ever logged. Fix: hasEssayClass now also matches c === 'essay' || c.indexOf('essay') === 0; result also includes || que.classList.contains('shortanswer'). AMD: tracker.js (src + build + min synced). No PHP, CSS, or DB schema changes. version.php → 2026051100149. // ADD-EG-CAPTURE-TEST: New capture_test.php live event capture diagnostic page at /plagiarism/essayguard/capture_test.php. Tests copy-paste detection, large inserts, keystroke ratio, backspace ratio, pause detection, and CPS simulation in real time. Mirrors analyser.php signal logic (S1/S2/S4/S5/S12/S13) in JS with live score prediction and false-positive cap indicator. No DB schema changes. // FIX-EG-S13-NO-PASTE (v1.2.143): Extend Signal 13 to also fire when JS events exist but contain no paste/large_insert AND keystroke ratio < 0.25. Previously Signal 13 (server-side CPS) was suppressed by even a single focus/modifier-key event ($events_empty_for_scoring=false), leaving copy-paste sessions stuck at ~45% MEDIUM instead of HIGH. FIX-EG-AGG-PASTE-MEANINGFUL (v1.2.143): $agg_has_paste_evidence in lib.php now requires Signal 1 >= 30 pts (meaningful paste) instead of any paste_events > 0. An incidental autocorrect paste (Signal 1 = 10 pts) was incorrectly triggering the per-question aggregate fallback, causing both Review Attempt questions to show the aggregate score (45%) while the EssayGuard Report showed the correct per-question scores (20%/0%) — a visible two-report mismatch. // FIX-EG-CFG-SCOPE (v1.2.142): TRUE ROOT CAUSE of all zero-event sessions. v1.2.141 added require_once($CFG->libdir . '/externallib.php') at file/namespace level in all three external class files. PHP scoping rule: when a file is included from inside a function (Moodle\'s spl_autoload_register classloader calls require_once($classfile) from inside the autoloader function), the included file\'s top-level code runs in that function\'s local scope — not the global scope. $CFG is a global variable and is therefore invisible at file level inside that function scope, causing a fatal PHP error on every AJAX call. tracker.js caught those errors silently in .catch() and rolled back — queue events were never spliced out and were eventually lost on page unload. Zero events ever reached plagiarism_essayguard_ev. Fix: added global $CFG; immediately before require_once($CFG->libdir . \'/externallib.php\') in all three files (log_event.php, finalize_attempt.php, get_badges.php). PHP-only. No AMD, CSS, DB schema changes. // // FIX-EG-EXTERNAL-API-CLASS (v1.2.141): ROOT CAUSE OF ALL ZERO-EVENT SESSIONS. Moodle 4.2+ moved external_api, external_function_parameters, external_value, external_single_structure, external_multiple_structure from the global namespace into \core_external\. The global aliases (e.g. 'external_api') only exist when lib/externallib.php is explicitly loaded via require_once. All three external function files (log_event.php, finalize_attempt.php, get_badges.php) were missing this require_once. Every AJAX call from tracker.js flush(), finalizeAttempt(), and reporter.js returned "Exception - Class external_api not found" (generalexceptionmessage). tracker.js caught those errors silently in the catch() block and rolled back — queue events were never spliced out and were eventually lost on page unload. Zero events ever reached plagiarism_essayguard_ev. All badges derived from linguistic fallback only = LOW. Fix: added require_once($CFG->libdir . '/externallib.php') to all three files, before the 'use external_api' declarations. PHP-only. No AMD, CSS, DB schema changes. // // FIX-EG-SINGLE-SENTENCE (v1.2.140): linguistic fallback awarded 0 pts for any single-sentence answer. linguistic::variance() correctly returns 0.0 for n<2 data points, but the fallback guarded on ($sentence_variance > 0.0) which therefore always failed for 1-sentence texts — the most common short-answer response format. A single sentence has perfect uniformity by definition and should earn the full +20 pts. Fix: replaced (> 0.0) guard with ($sentence_count_ling >= 1), extracted from $linguistic['sentence_count']. PHP-only change (analyser.php). No AMD, CSS, DB schema, or other file changes. // // FIX-EG-BADGE-DIAG-QSLOT-COL (v1.2.139): badge_diag.php crashed on load with a DB exception. The raw-event query used ORDER BY qslot ASC on plagiarism_essayguard_ev, but that table has NO qslot column (qslot is stored inside payloadjson for each event; the qslot column only exists on plagiarism_essayguard_sc). Fix: ORDER BY changed to eventtime ASC only; qslot extracted from decoded payloadjson in PHP after fetch. PHP-only change (badge_diag.php). No AMD, CSS, DB schema, or other file changes. version.php → 2026051000142. // FIX-EG-TRACKER-UNLOCK-GATE (v1.2.138): inject_tracker() was gated on check_unlock(). When a site has Site ID + API Key configured but the license server returns unlocked=false (auto-unlock failed due to insufficient credits), inject_tracker() returned early with no AMD call. The JS tracker never loaded, zero events reached plagiarism_essayguard_ev, and every submission fell back to linguistic-only scoring (30% MEDIUM baseline). The unlock gate has been removed from inject_tracker() — event capture is now unconditional (events are audit data, not credit-consuming). Scoring gates remain in observer.php is_active(), finalize_attempt.php execute(), and log_event.php. FIX-EG-DIAG-RETRY-CHECK (v1.2.138): diag.php Section 4 checked for a named retryBind() function that never existed — the implementation uses anonymous setTimeout callbacks. False FAIL on every install of v1.2.114+. Check updated to look for setTimeout values 300/1200/2500 + MutationObserver presence. FIX-EG-DIAG-IDENTICAL-SCORE (v1.2.138): diag.php Section 5 falsely flagged Bug 1 when per-question scores were identical but differed from the aggregate — actually expected when zero JS events cause identical linguistic fallback scores. Now only fails when per-question scores equal the aggregate (true qslot-detection fallback). PHP-only. No AMD, CSS, DB schema, or JS changes. version.php → 2026051000141. // FIX-EG-GLOBAL-DB-NULL (v1.2.135): on_quiz_attempt_submitted() missing global $DB — crashed with "Call to a member function get_record() on null" on every quiz submit. CLEAN-EG-OBSERVER-DIAG: 5 production error_log() calls removed (observer.php lines 125-129 quiz_attempt_submitted PII log, line 143 slot_texts count log, line 375 responsesummary fallback log, line 391 fallback-used log; analyser.php lines 78-81 score_attempt event-count DEBUG log). PHP-only change. No AMD, CSS, or DB schema changes. version.php -> 2026051000138. // CLEAN-EG-PROD-DIAG (v1.2.134): Three production error_log() calls removed from lib.php get_links() — fired on every student/teacher page load for every question on every quiz attempt, flooding the server log with PII (userid, cmid, riskscore) on every normal operation. (1) Per-question DB fetch log (qslot+riskscore). (2) Aggregate DB fetch log (riskscore). (3) No-record-found log (userid+cmid+qslot). PHP-only change. No AMD, CSS, or DB schema changes. version.php → 2026051000137. // FIX-EG-BADGE-LEVEL (v1.2.133): buildBadgeEl() palette lookup bug — `palette[data.risklevel] || 'low'` returned the colour object (truthy), not the string key. `palette[object]` then returned undefined, so c.border/c.bg/c.text were all undefined and every risk badge rendered with no colour. Fix: `(data.risklevel in palette) ? data.risklevel : 'low'` — correctly returns the string key. FIX-EG-ORPHAN-SYNTAX (v1.2.133): tracker.js lines 1277-1278 contained an orphaned string expression with a stray `)` (leftover from a deleted console.log call during CLEAN-EG-TRACKER-2 v1.2.130). The unmatched `)` is a JavaScript SyntaxError that prevents the AMD module from loading, silently disabling all EssayGuard telemetry. Both lines removed from src, build, and min. AMD: tracker.js (src + build + min synced). No PHP, CSS, or DB schema changes. version.php → 2026051000136. // FIX-EG-MISSED-PERQ-PASTE (v1.2.132): lib.php fallback condition extended. Original guard fired only on riskscore=0.0. Common real-world case missed: Ctrl+V paste records 2 keydown events tagged to the slot, but the paste/large_insert event lands on the aggregate pool — per-question scorer finds keystrokes, no paste, FIX-EG-TYPING-FALSE-POSITIVE caps score to 29 (riskscore=0.29 > 0.0) — old guard never triggered. EssayGuard Report (aggregate) showed HIGH; Review Attempt badge (per-question) showed LOW — visible mismatch. Fix: also fall back to aggregate when riskscore < 0.30 AND paste_events = 0 AND total_keystrokes <= 10 AND aggregate has paste evidence. Honest typists who typed Q2 while Q1 was pasted are protected because their total_keystrokes >> 10. No DB schema changes. version.php -> 2026051000135. // CLEAN-EG-TRACKER-3 (v1.2.131): Third dead-code pass — removed dead local var diagId in cacheQslot (assigned node.id, never subsequently read; was a leftover debug capture from v1.2.77 DIAG-EG-QSLOT-DIAG). tracker.js: 1839→1544 lines (−295 total). No logic changes. version.php->2026051000134. // CLEAN-EG-TRACKER-2 (v1.2.130): Second dead-code pass — removed showPasteWarning (115 lines, never called since v1.2.64 paste-always-allow), clearWarningOnTyping (16 lines, corollary), state.allowpaste prop (never read), 13 blocks of orphaned JS string-expression remnants left when console.log calls were removed (DIAG-EG-FLUSH, FIX-EG-QSLOT-DIAG, DIAG-EG-BIND, bind-qslot debug, isTypedAnswerField skip, bindTinyMCENode skip, DIAG-EG-SCAN + dead _diagFound var + empty forEach, scan qtype skip, FIX-EG-INIT-DIAG, finalizeAttempt result log). tracker.js: 1839→1547 lines (−292 total). No logic changes. // CLEAN-EG-TRACKER (v1.2.129): Dead code removed — 5 stale global state props (lastKeyTime/wordCountWindow/windowStartTime/windowWordCount/cursorMoves, replaced by per-field vars in v1.2.36), legacy palette aliases (partial/mild) from buildBadgeEl and restorePendingBadge, 20+ DIAG console.log statements, verbose multi-paragraph FIX-* comments trimmed to single-line. FIX-EG-TMCE-LOADBIND (v1.2.128): New per-attempt diagnostic page attempt_diag.php at /plagiarism/essayguard/attempt_diag.php?cmid=X&userid=Y&attemptkey=Z. Shows every stored event in plagiarism_essayguard_ev with event type, time offset, qslot resolved from payload, and key payload fields (insertlen, delta, ikd, etc.); qslot routing audit explaining which events went to which slot and why; per-slot metric grid (paste_events, large_inserts, keystrokes, backspaces, paste_chars_total, keystroke_ratio, etc.); signal-by-signal breakdown drawn from stored metricsjson signal_breakdown (S1–S13 with points, FIRED/silent status, and plain-English explanation of why each fired including the threshold and actual metric value); false-positive cap status; final score100 with band; and automated diagnosis flags (zero-paste, zero-keystroke, no qslot tags, score/evidence mismatch). Student and attemptkey pickers allow switching without leaving the page. Linked from diag.php. Requires moodle/site:config or plagiarism/essayguard:viewreport. Read-only — no external requests. No DB schema changes. version.php → 2026051000134.
// VERSION BUMP (v1.2.126): TWO ROOT-CAUSE FIXES for copy-paste being badged MEDIUM instead of HIGH. (1) FIX-EG-PASTE-IMMEDIATE-FLUSH: tracker.js paste and drop handlers now call flush() immediately after queuing the event. Previously only the 5-second periodic flush sent events to the server; a student who pasted and submitted within 5 seconds left paste_events=0 in the DB, forcing the linguistic fallback (which cannot detect well-written copy-paste) and producing a MEDIUM badge instead of HIGH. Fix applied to all three paste capture paths: plain textarea addEventListener paste, the drop handler, and the TinyMCE document-level capture-phase paste handler. (2) FIX-EG-SERVER-TIMING: analyser.php now accepts attempt_timestart and attempt_timefinish from observer.php (fetched from quiz_attempts) and computes server-side chars-per-second when JS events are absent. If server_cps > 10 (physically impossible to type 120 WPM sustained over the whole attempt duration) → Signal 13 adds +50 pts → HIGH. If > 4 cps (48 WPM sustained) → +25 pts → MEDIUM-HIGH. Stored as server_cps in metricsjson for diag.php visibility. No DB schema changes.
